{"skill":{"slug":"blog-writer","displayName":"Blog Writer"},"version":{"version":"0.1.0","createdAt":1769361436760,"changelog":"blog-writer 0.1.0 released\n\n- Initial release introducing a skill for writing authentic, opinionated blog posts and articles in the writer’s distinctive voice.\n- Handles the complete workflow: research review, drafting, style matching, iterative feedback, and automatic publication to Notion.\n- Ensures every draft is published to the TS Notes Notion database with correct metadata (Type=Writing, Project=My Writing).\n- Finalized posts are saved to a versioned examples library for future style calibration.\n- Includes detailed guidelines for writing style, structure, length, and vocabulary.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"2024-02-17-radical-transparency-sales.md","size":3543,"sha256":"c166b58ffa9bc647766e7e6f7ed5064ef9087c8792d3bba220fc0933abf668f4","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"2024-02-17-raycast-spotlight-superpowers.md","size":2984,"sha256":"e294c6c3f7914161b3a5edd9d83c88ed548b3ac0c49b365e05064b0dc7b2c194","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"2024-02-17-short-form-content-marketing.md","size":5125,"sha256":"c0db69d205a1ad77c0d6d117861372bf4f2ea710bca7874da8c8a02163dca188","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"2024-02-17-typing-speed-benefits.md","size":3453,"sha256":"a428f8530ca46992acac5e1bcecc99003c4a000e09939084475090e5d85a9a57","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"2024-03-14-effective-ai-prompts.md","size":3524,"sha256":"258f9888102735cc957523f529f9735b4a084b0c1e6f32b5d1a35d5449b44e6e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"2024-11-08-ai-revolutionizing-entry-level-sales.md","size":5317,"sha256":"65f6c00a98649623c5fd5a2adca34a9f9efeac63eab61c76a6475117fd95cdf6","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"2025-11-12-why-ai-art-is-useless.md","size":5783,"sha256":"20244737af79193961e0e6e3aab413a9921c3a0be4548b7b3b1bc5061bc0ff5a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"README.md","size":189,"sha256":"b5362bb0cb00fc233a4691b74f991ba227f43dba5cf25b2c9b987b0bc1f4bd5d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6924,"sha256":"6e6391cf989d16c8ef26f6a941704664f490ff917918eb7ac96c01085bb362dc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"manage_examples.py","size":2643,"sha256":"b879665b2cb1aae3f7ad7438212f7694834ba494535465e52573206f63cfb966","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"style-guide.md","size":6323,"sha256":"5536121bcb17b61848ab06e79f07ce27a5146d5dd76575e59c7e7b6180bfdd85","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2395,"sha256":"6900f772add588578dfb3a0d2200e9785b6923a93b849307bd843821a26c2816","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789018249485,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9b8402e8b45f56e186af06c71457ccc56bc9f8da93d101671e98105d3019c00e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9b8402e8b45f56e186af06c71457ccc56bc9f8da93d101671e98105d3019c00e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: blog-writer\nVersion: 0.1.0\n\nThe skill is designed to write blog posts, publish them to a specified Notion database, and manage a local library of example posts. It involves an external API call to Notion for publishing and local file system operations (read, write, delete) within the skill's `references/blog-examples` directory for managing its internal knowledge base. While these are high-risk capabilities in general, they are explicitly stated in `SKILL.md` and `manage_examples.py`, and are directly aligned with the skill's stated purpose. There is no evidence of intentional harmful behavior, data exfiltration beyond the stated Notion publication, or unauthorized command execution.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159951559},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":85,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789018249485},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a blog-writing helper, but it requires sending draft content to a fixed Notion database without a fresh user confirmation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill assumes access to a specific Notion destination and could transmit user notes, research, and unfinished drafts to a third-party workspace, which is broader than needed for local drafting.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency setup, remote payload retrieval, or automatic execution was found; the included Python utility is a local example-library helper.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Activation covers broad blog/article and research-note requests, then treats external publication as required even for drafts, without requiring per-action approval.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persists content externally in Notion and locally in an examples library; local pruning is permission-gated, but Notion persistence is mandatory and under-scoped.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The writing and style-matching functions fit the stated purpose, but mandatory Notion publication of full draft content is a high-impact side effect for ordinary writing requests.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want this skill to publish writing to the configured Notion database as part of its normal workflow. Do not use it for private notes, sensitive research, or unfinished drafts unless you first edit the skill to require explicit confirmation before every Notion write and to verify the destination.","findings":"[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: SKILL.md requires publishing complete draft content to a hardcoded Notion database and says non-publication is failure.\n[T05] unexpected: Accepted in substance: the static scan's external-publication concern is supported by the required Notion workflow, though no credential theft or privilege escalation was found.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Accepted as contributing context: broad writing triggers become riskier because they automatically lead to external publication.\n[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the example-management script aligns with the declared examples-library maintenance workflow and deletes only when run with an explicit execute flag; it is not the primary concern.\n[MP3] expected: Overridden: the cited text is an example blog post about prompt writing, not an instruction to alter agent memory or persistent state.\n[RA2] expected: Overridden: the cited voice-and-tone text is not a cron job, startup item, plist, or background persistence mechanism.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789018249485}}}}}